# Changelog

Breaking changes, migration guides, and notable updates from the pinned COSS reference.

<CopyMarkdownButton url="/docs/changelog.md" />

The dates and topics below match the upstream COSS changelog. Commands and examples are translated to
the Svelte registry where the same change applies. Entries tied only to the upstream framework are
kept as provenance notes instead of prescribing an unrelated Svelte migration.

## August 19, 2026

### Tabs sizing and segmented control styles

**`Tabs.List`** supports a **`size`** prop with **`"sm"`**, **`"default"`**, and **`"lg"`** values.
The size propagates to its **`Tabs.Tab`** children, and an individual tab can override the inherited
size.

The default Tabs appearance uses the same optical item sizing as the
[Segmented Control](/docs/components/segmented-control) pattern. The default rendered height is
slightly smaller so the inset active indicator stays balanced beside a Button of the corresponding
size.

Tabs shares its item layout and size maps with the Segmented Control implementation. The registry
records that dependency, so shadcn-svelte installs it with a fresh Tabs installation.

**Migration:**

Existing Tabs markup needs no size prop because `"default"` remains the default. If you replace a
local Tabs component through the CLI, review local changes before accepting the overwrite:

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/tabs.json
```

After updating, remove local height or horizontal-padding utilities only where they accidentally
override the new size API. Keep intentional product-specific overrides. Verify the default and
underline variants at every size used by the application.

## July 31, 2026

### Scroll Area — overscroll contain

**`ScrollArea.Root`** no longer applies **`overscroll-behavior: contain`** by default. Use the optional
**`overscrollContain`** prop, whose default is **`false`**, to opt in.

Nested surfaces that must not chain scroll to the page already pass it, including dialog, sheet,
drawer, combobox, autocomplete, and sidebar panels.

**Migration:**

No change is required for those composed parts after upgrading. For custom nested scroll areas, opt
in explicitly:

```diff
- <ScrollArea.Root scrollbarGutter scrollFade>
+ <ScrollArea.Root overscrollContain scrollbarGutter scrollFade>
```

Add the prop only where wheel or touch scrolling should not propagate to a parent scroller.

## July 26, 2026

### Calendar engine update

The upstream COSS release moved its framework-specific DayPicker dependency to version 10 and removed
APIs deprecated in version 9.

COSS for Svelte does not use that package. Its Calendar adapter uses the Svelte implementation in this
repository and `@internationalized/date` values. No dependency or import migration is required. If
you maintain a custom Calendar wrapper, compare it to the current
[Calendar documentation](/docs/components/calendar) and tests instead of applying the upstream
framework migration literally.

## June 22, 2026

### Behavioral primitive update

The upstream COSS release updated Base UI and renamed an OTP namespace export. COSS for Svelte uses
Shards UI, so the Base UI package and namespace rename do not apply.

The Svelte OTP module exposes the COSS parts through its namespace. Update generated files from the
Svelte registry when the local API differs:

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/otp-field.json
```

## June 11, 2026

### Context Menu

**Context Menu** is the pointer-anchored action-menu component for right click and long press. See the
[Context Menu documentation](/docs/components/context-menu) for installation and examples.

**Install:**

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/context-menu.json
```

There is no migration from an earlier COSS primitive. Use it where pointer-triggered actions belong
beside, or instead of, a regular Menu.

### Menu and Context Menu — link items

**`Menu.LinkItem`** and **`ContextMenu.LinkItem`** are styled navigation rows. They match the action
items visually and close the menu after navigation by default.

Use link items for navigation and action items for callbacks:

```diff
- <Menu.Item onclick={() => goto("/docs")}>Docs</Menu.Item>
+ <Menu.LinkItem href="/docs">Docs</Menu.LinkItem>
```

For a SvelteKit-enhanced anchor, keep the anchor attributes on the link item. Do not translate the
upstream render-delegation example; Svelte components accept native anchor attributes directly.

```svelte
<Menu.LinkItem data-sveltekit-preload-data="hover" href="/docs">Docs</Menu.LinkItem>
```

The equivalent Context Menu migration changes only the namespace:

```diff
- <ContextMenu.Item onclick={() => goto("/docs")}>Docs</ContextMenu.Item>
+ <ContextMenu.LinkItem href="/docs">Docs</ContextMenu.LinkItem>
```

## May 29, 2026

### Scroll Area

**`ScrollArea.Root`** adds an optional **`fill`** prop whose default is **`false`**. When enabled,
`size-full` is applied to the content so inner flex layouts can use the full viewport height, such as
pinning a footer with `mt-auto` in a sidebar.

Most scroll areas should keep the default. Opt in only when the scroll container must stretch rather
than size to its children.

**Migration:**

No change is required for lists, dialogs, comboboxes, or command menus. For a flex column with a
bottom-pinned footer, opt in explicitly:

```diff
- <ScrollArea.Root class="min-h-0 flex-1">
+ <ScrollArea.Root class="min-h-0 flex-1" fill>
    <div class="flex h-full flex-col">
      ...
      <footer class="mt-auto">...</footer>
    </div>
  </ScrollArea.Root>
```

The generated Sidebar content already passes `fill`; update its registry item if your project owns an
older copy.

## April 17, 2026

### Form

The **`Form`** component no longer applies default layout classes. It is a thin behavioral wrapper;
pass `class` wherever you need a vertical field stack, width constraints, or dialog layout.

**Migration:**

Restore a typical stacked layout explicitly:

```diff
- <Form onsubmit={save}>
+ <Form class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4" onsubmit={save}>
```

For dialogs, sheets, and drawers, keep the Header outside the form. Wrap the Panel and Footer in a
Form, or a native form, with `class="contents"`. Display contents keeps the header, panel, and footer
as direct flex children so panel scroll and height constraints continue to work.

```svelte
<Dialog.Popup>
  <Dialog.Header>...</Dialog.Header>
  <form class="contents" onsubmit={save}>
    <Dialog.Panel>...</Dialog.Panel>
    <Dialog.Footer>...</Dialog.Footer>
  </form>
</Dialog.Popup>
```

## April 14, 2026

### OTP Field

The earlier Input OTP registry item was replaced by **OTP Field**. See the
[OTP Field documentation](/docs/components/otp-field) and
[migration guide](/docs/radix-migration#otp-field) for the current namespace.

**Migration:**

```diff
- pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/input-otp.json
+ pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/otp-field.json
```

```diff
- import * as InputOTP from "$lib/components/ui/input-otp/index.js";
+ import * as OTPField from "$lib/components/ui/otp-field/index.js";
```

Use `OTPField.Root`, `OTPField.Input`, and `OTPField.Separator`, and set `length` on the root.

## April 12, 2026

### Table

`Table` supports an optional **`variant`** prop: **`"default"`**, which is the default, or
**`"card"`**. Omitting it keeps the earlier appearance. Use `variant="card"` for the separated-row
grid shown in the [Table documentation](/docs/components/table), including tables inside Frame or
Card Frame.

**Migration:**

Existing tables require no change. Opt in only where the design calls for the card-style grid:

```svelte
<Table variant="card">...</Table>
```

## March 20, 2026

### Toggle Group

The grouped item is named `ToggleGroup.Item` to avoid a conflict with the standalone `Toggle` export.

**Migration:**

```diff
- import { Toggle, ToggleGroup } from "$lib/components/ui/toggle-group/index.js";
+ import * as ToggleGroup from "$lib/components/ui/toggle-group/index.js";
```

```diff
- <ToggleGroup>
-   <Toggle value="bold">Bold</Toggle>
- </ToggleGroup>
+ <ToggleGroup.Root>
+   <ToggleGroup.Item value="bold">Bold</ToggleGroup.Item>
+ </ToggleGroup.Root>
```

Do not change imports from the standalone Toggle module.
